⍝ regression (Bugs28 #74): 1⎕TF of a lambda used to write out
⍝ canonical() of the lambda under its own header (λ←λ1 ⍵, say) and, on
⍝ the way back in, "fix" that text under the header's own synthetic
⍝ name -- redefining λ1 instead of the name the caller assigned to,
⍝ leaving the original name a VALUE ERROR. 1⎕TF now refuses a lambda
⍝ outright, matching 2⎕TF's existing refusal (Bugs27 #52). Same for a
⍝ lambda operator.
⍝
      )ERASE L
      L←{⍵+1}
      1 ⎕TF 'L'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1 ⎕TF 'L'
      ^     ^

      )MORE
⎕TF: 'L' is a lambda (dfn); lambdas cannot be written to a transfer-format (.atf) file or produced by ⎕TF, since other APL systems (and GNU APL's own transfer-format reader) have no way to represent them. Use ⎕FX-style named functions for anything that needs to survive )OUT/)IN or ⎕TF.

      2 ⎕TF 'L'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      2 ⎕TF 'L'
      ^     ^

      )MORE
)OUT/⎕TF: 'L' is a lambda (dfn); lambdas cannot be written to a transfer-format (.atf) file or produced by ⎕TF, since other APL systems (and GNU APL's own transfer-format reader) have no way to represent them. Use ⎕FX-style named functions for anything that needs to survive )OUT/)IN or ⎕TF.

      )ERASE M
      M←{⍺⍺ ⍵}
      1 ⎕TF 'M'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1 ⎕TF 'M'
      ^     ^

      2 ⎕TF 'M'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      2 ⎕TF 'M'
      ^     ^

      )SIC

      )ERASE L
      )ERASE M

⍝ regression (Bugs28 #75): )OUT of a workspace containing a lambda used
⍝ to abort entirely -- Symbol::write_OUT let Quad_TF::tf2_fun_ucs's
⍝ DOMAIN ERROR propagate uncaught while looping over all symbols,
⍝ silently truncating the .atf file to whatever had been written before
⍝ the lambda was reached. )OUT now skips a lambda with a CERR-only
⍝ warning (like the existing )SAVE warning for a dirty SI) and keeps
⍝ writing the rest of the workspace.
⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )DROP dwout75.atf
³

      F1←{⌽⍵}
      X75←42
      )OUT dwout75

      data ← ⎕FIO[26] 'workspaces/dwout75.atf'
      ~∨/'F1' ⍷ data
1
      ∨/'X75' ⍷ data
1

      )DROP dwout75.atf
³

